# Example: restrict direct access to recordings by client IP (nginx).
# Product default: location /data/ in standalone.conf.template serves all of /app/data/.
# Threat: predictable paths .../recordings/YYYY/MM/DD/HHMMSS/video.mp4 without HTTP auth.
#
# How to use:
# 1) Merge into server { } in the generated default.conf (after entrypoint), or maintain a fork
#    of standalone.conf.template for your host.
# 2) Replace allow lines with your LAN/VPN CIDRs. Test: curl -I from allowed vs denied IP.
# 3) Longer prefix ^~ /data/recordings/ wins over location /data/ for recording URLs.
#
# Optional: keep generic location /data/ for images/db paths — only recordings are allowlisted
# here; other /data/* still follow the next location /data/ block (tune deny rules if needed).

# location ^~ /data/recordings/ {
#     alias /app/data/recordings/;
#     autoindex off;
#     add_header Accept-Ranges bytes;
#     allow 127.0.0.1;
#     allow 192.168.0.0/16;
#     allow 10.0.0.0/8;
#     deny all;
# }
